WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.149
Diagram Studio: explore different outcomes on one technical diagram. No account required.

2
00:00:06.149 --> 00:00:18.145
A read request enters the API, then checks Redis before querying PostgreSQL.

3
00:00:18.145 --> 00:00:24.094
Redis times out. The reader chooses how the API responds. Timing figures are illustrative.

4
00:00:24.094 --> 00:00:31.103
Choice 1: fall back to PostgreSQL. Keep reads available, at the cost of extra database load and latency.

5
00:00:31.103 --> 00:00:38.103
The request succeeds with HTTP 200. The notes explain the capacity tradeoff.

6
00:00:38.103 --> 00:00:43.080
Reuse the same diagram to explore a different outcome.

7
00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:50.083
Choice 2: return HTTP 503. Protect database capacity, but this request fails.

8
00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:56.070
A bounded retry with backoff may help later. Uncontrolled retries could make the outage worse.

9
00:00:56.070 --> 00:01:03.124
Restart resets the walkthrough and requires a new choice.

10
00:01:03.124 --> 00:01:14.086
Remix creates an independent browser-local copy. Edit it without changing the original example.

11
00:01:14.086 --> 00:01:18.358
The hosted demo keeps edits in this browser. Export JSON for a portable, editable backup.

12
00:01:18.358 --> 00:01:26.007
Full-version account saves, revisions and publications remain in the project and its tests; they are disabled in this hosted guest demo.
